  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PatPre2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'You hear that a new potential treatment has shown strong promise in
    early studies, which makes you hopeful, but it has yet to be tested in people.
    The research team is conducting preclinical studies in mice before moving forward
    to trials.

    

    <b>Preclinical research helps researchers determine whether
    a new treatment is safe enough to be tested in people..</b>

    Is this <b>true</b>
    or <b>false</b>?'
  explanation: Before a new treatment is tested in people, researchers use lab and
    animal studies to learn how it behaves in the body and to look for possible safety
    concerns. This step helps protect patients by making sure only treatments that
    appear safe enough move forward into clinical trials. It also reduces the risk
    of unexpected harm once people are involved.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: PreClinical
